 ## Listing and queries
 
+`Get` and `List` release member-only information only while the loaded signed
+identity still has read permission. `Status` and `Stats` apply the same guard
+to the member surface's local diagnostics. Each materializes its result outside
+ACL/lifetime locks, then checks the same signed head and captured account/Space
+generation before releasing it. A removed identity receives a permission error
+and no result even if historical read keys and bytes remain cached locally.
+Already delivered information is not erased.
+
+`SubscribeStatus` captures the current loaded generation without loading a
+Space. Each local event is admitted against that same identity, signed head and
+lifetime immediately before external callback invocation. Queued events that
+observe removal, cancellation or retirement are withheld; quiescing events are
+dropped because this is a best-effort stream. An already admitted callback may
+finish after cancellation or retirement. User callbacks run outside every ACL,
+lifetime and subscription-admission lock, and unsubscribe does not promise to
+drain external callback execution. A changed authority generation requires a
+new subscription; `Status` remains the point-in-time recovery path.
+
+The raw `Query`/live-query and `PayloadsView` surfaces retain their separate
+node-readable contract. They expose the original cleartext index and sealed
+`enc` blob, not unsealed member metadata. Their existing owner-deletion checks
+are unchanged.
+
 - `List(opts)` — typed `FileInfo`s; `ObjectId` is the indexed fast path,
   `Limit` caps the result. An unfiltered listing walks every file in the
   space; large-space consumers page or use `Query` / `Changes`.
